nodecode-devtune is a rewrite of devtunehq's devtunehq/skills:

  https://github.com/devtunehq/skills
  commit bb38e20a34a7577d359fd9a508caa1cf1ef8b1a7

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 DevTune (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin had no code at all -- an MCP server entry and two
skill prompts -- so the two tables those prompts carry, one read a line, are this
cell's report table: the same REST paths under https://devtune.ai/api/v2, the same
project key as a bearer header, the same reads (connection, visibility summary and
diff, competitive position, top citation domains and pages, visibility responses and
one response, content gaps and their evidence, traffic summary, platforms, AI
referrals and 404 demand, actions and one action's brief, audit summary and findings,
the outcomes ledger, and the nine Agent Picks reads with their setup). The skills'
guidance -- what a percentage is against a fraction, a citation against a mention,
not-measured against zero, a pick rate against an install rate, an outcome against a
cause -- is the manual topic, and the reads are the model's tool. What was left out:
the MCP server itself, the write and credit-spending calls (prompts, competitors,
briefs, drafts, test starts) and the agent-driven signup, so a model reading through
this cell cannot change a project or spend a credit; and the JSON prelude a hosted
server wrapped its answers in, this cell answering DevTune's own JSON under one line
naming the read.
